1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,601
Travel Memory Map — Group 21. Real cloud Qwen; synthetic data; assistant-operated demo.

2
00:00:04,601 --> 00:00:07,783
Input: select Osaka and enter notes. The image is synthetic; city is a user label.

3
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:12,669
Saving a trip lights the city and creates a separate local record.

4
00:00:12,669 --> 00:00:18,217
Before upload, the app discloses this trip only: city, date, title, notes and one photo.

5
00:00:18,217 --> 00:00:20,853
Processing: one real cloud request to qwen3.8-flash. No stored trip is overwritten.

6
00:00:20,853 --> 00:00:27,984
Output: an editable AI draft. It is not saved automatically.

7
00:00:27,984 --> 00:00:32,156
Edit the draft, then explicitly save. This automated demo is not a human quality rating.

8
00:00:32,156 --> 00:00:42,072
Reload verification: the edited memory persists; the visit count remains one.

9
00:00:42,072 --> 00:00:50,983
Boundary case: a second trip says the sign reads OPEN, but its image says CLOSED.

10
00:00:50,983 --> 00:00:55,615
Real cloud boundary test: the model must not silently choose between conflicting facts.

11
00:00:55,615 --> 00:01:04,361
The model asks for clarification. The saved trip remains unchanged; no invented memory is
saved.

12
00:01:04,361 --> 00:01:11,208
Two saved trips, one city. Reload preserves both records. Human quality review is still
pending.
